# "Whenever a land YOU control enters": Bloodghast sits in Bot1's graveyard (Lightning Bolt, turn 2). Bot2 playing an
# Island on turn 4 asks Bot1 nothing (refusal, placed after the pass that takes the priority a trigger would have given),
# and the Bloodghast is still in the graveyard at the start of turn 5, when Bot1's own Island brings it back (the positive
# control).

[Bot1 Deck]
Swamp
Mox Jet
Bloodghast
Island
Island x16

[Bot2 Deck]
Mountain
Lightning Bolt
Island
Island x17

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Swamp.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Swamp.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Bloodghast.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot2.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Bloodghast)
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Pass
! Bot1.Accept
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
? Bot1.Graveyard = Bloodghast
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Accept
[T5 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Graveyard.Count = 0
Bot1.Battlefield = Swamp; Mox Jet; Island; Bloodghast
